.TH CLIPBRIDGE 1 clipbridge\-VERSION
.SH NAME
clipbridge \- clipboard listener and daemon powered by unipaste
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clipbridge
.RB [ \-w1pruv ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR mode ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR table ]
.RB [ \-l
.IR link ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clipbridge
monitors the system clipboard for rich HTML updates, formats the HTML using the
\fBunipaste\fR engine, and updates the clipboard plain-text slot.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B \-w
Watch the system clipboard in the background (default).
.TP
.B \-1
Format current clipboard once and exit.
.TP
.B \-p
Print formatted clipboard text to stdout.
.SH FORMATTING OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-m " mode"
Output mode: \fBplain\fR (default), \fBmarkdown\fR, or \fBterminal\fR.
.TP
.BI \-t " table"
Table format: \fBgrid\fR (default), \fBmarkdown\fR, \fBtsv\fR, or \fBsimple\fR.
.TP
.BI \-l " link"
Link format: \fBbracket\fR (default), \fBinline\fR, \fBtext\fR, or \fBfootnote\fR.
.TP
.B \-u
Use Unicode box-drawing characters for tables.
.TP
.B \-r
Emit Windows CRLF (\\r\\n) line endings.
.TP
.B \-v
Display version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h
Display help message and exit.
